CHALLENGE #1: GOALS
• Create a simple, organized, and easy-to-navigate student dashboard.
• Use semantic and properly structured HTML elements to organize the page.
• Apply CSS colors, fonts, spacing, borders, and backgrounds to make the design clear and 
consistent.
• Use Flexbox to arrange the sidebar and main content area.
• Practice linking pages or sections and using images, lists, and tables where appropriate.
• Improve my ability to write, organize, test, and troubleshoot HTML and CSS code.

PLANS

1. Plan the layout
Identify the dashboard sections and sketch 
how the sidebar and main content will be
arranged

2. Build with HTML
Create the page structure using headings, 
paragraphs, links, lists, images, and tables 
as needed.

3. Style with CSS
Add colors, typography, spacing, borders, 
backgrounds, and a consistent visual theme

4. Arrange the layout
Use Flexbox and appropriate sizing to 
position the sidebar and dashboard 
content.

5. Test and Improve
Preview the website in a browser, check 
links and alignment, fix errors, and refine 
the design.
